# redirect-farm — a config built of `return` directives, which are
# parse-only at this pin: the chain notes NAME that above the 404
# decision (never a silently wrong redirect prediction).
args: --request 'GET http://old.example.org/blog/post'
exit: 0
--- expect
== request: GET http://old.example.org/blog/post
listener: 127.0.0.1:8080
server: tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:16 [server_name old.example.org legacy.example.org] — its server_name matches the request's host (exact, then the longest leading wildcard, then the longest trailing one)
  candidate server tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:10 [server_name example.org] — lost: not chosen for this listener and host (another server block answers it)
location: / (tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:28)
  precedence: = exact > longest prefix (regex is parse-only at this pin and never wins)
  candidate location /old-blog/ (tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:20) — lost: the path does not start with this prefix
  candidate location = /promo (tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:24) — lost: the path is not exactly this location's `=` argument
  candidate location / (tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:28) — won: the longest matching prefix wins (1 bytes)
effective directives (the winning chain, with provenance):
  listen 8080;  # from tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:17
  server_name old.example.org legacy.example.org;  # from tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:18
  rewrite ^(.*[^/])$ $1/ permanent;  # from tests/config-corpus/redirect-farm/nginx.conf:29
  note: parsed but not implemented at this pin, so they do not shape this decision: `rewrite` (statuses: docs/directives.md)
decision: would answer 404 — no root/alias maps this path to the filesystem — the live server answers 404
